<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matchlock</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The matchlock was an early firearm mechanism in which a slow-burning match was lowered onto the priming powder to fire the gun. Matchlock <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">muskets</a> spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurasia">Eurasia</a> in the sixteenth century. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, musketeers armed with matchlocks fought alongside cavalry and artillery.</p></div>
